mes>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Prenatal window of susceptibility to perfluorooctane sulfonate-induced neonatal mortality in the Sprague-Dawley rat</article-title><source>Birth Defects Res B Dev Reprod Toxicol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14745980</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ehp0115-001677"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grice</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Alexander</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffbeck</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kampa</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Self-Reported medical conditions in perfluorooctanesulfonyl fluoride manufacturing workers</article-title><source>J Occup Environ Med</source><volume>49</volume><fpage>722</fpage><lpage>729</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17622844</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ehp0115-001677"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Perfluorooctanoic acid and perfluorononanoic acid in fetal and neonatal mice following <italic>in utero</italic> exposure to 8-2 fluorotelomer alcohol</article-title><source>Toxicol Sci</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>452</fpage><lpage>461</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17093205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ehp0115-001677"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hinderliter</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mylchreest</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gannon</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Butenhoff</surname><